@startuml CheckPermission Sequence

title Check Permission API Sequence

' Leading SQL apostrophes use &#39; so PlantUML preserves literals; parity compares decoded SQL.

' Visual style
skinparam defaultFontName "Sarabun"
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #475569
    ArrowFontColor #334155
    LifeLineBorderColor #CBD5E1
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    ParticipantBorderColor #94A3B8
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
    ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
    GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
    GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    GroupFontColor #334155
}

' Do not show participant footers at the bottom of the diagram
hide footbox
actor "User" as user
box "Frontend" #F8FAFC
    participant "Check Permission Page" as page
end box
box "Web API" #F8FAFC
    participant "API" as api
    participant "Application" as app
    participant "Domain" as domain
    participant "Infrastructure" as infra
end box
box "Database" #F8FAFC
    database "t_user_access_token" as t_user_access_token
end box
user -> page: Ask whether my token holds a permission (and a scope)
activate page
page -> api: GET v1/author/check?permission=&scope= (Bearer JWT, timestamp, requestId)
activate api
api -> app: [**CheckPermissionQueryHandler**] Process request
activate app
app -> app: Generate requestId if omitted; validate mandatory UTC timestamp and the query keys permission (mandatory) and scope (optional)
note over app, infra
    Validate mandatory timestamp as a UTC timestamp before SQL. Accept only the single query keys permission and
    scope, no body. permission is mandatory, at most 64 characters, lower-case letters, digits, `_` and `.` with
    exactly one `:` before the action part (`^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*(\.[a-z0-9_]+)*:[a-z0-9_]+$`), the claim form of a
    permission name whose last `.` becomes `:`. scope is optional, at most 64 characters, `<lower-case scope
    code>:*` (`^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*:\*$`). Missing/repeated/unknown keys, an empty value or a wrong format return
    400 E10001 before SQL. Generate requestId if omitted.
    Missing/malformed Bearer credentials or a failed JWT signature/issuer/audience/expiry/UUID sub validation
    return the same 401 E10002 `Invalid or expired access token.` before SQL. Validate the claims of the payload
    defined by [login](../../authen-and-author/02-login/spec.md#example-jwt-payload) (owner-confirmed
    2026-11-13): `roles`, `permissions` and `scopes` must each be an array of unique non-empty strings, including
    explicit []. A missing or malformed claim makes the credential invalid (401); never replace it with an empty
    list or recover privileges from the database.
end note
alt Missing or malformed timestamp or query
    app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001
    api -> page: Validation error
else Valid headers and query
    app -> app: Verify JWT signature/issuer/audience/exp/UUID sub and the roles, permissions and scopes claims as arrays of unique non-empty strings
    alt Missing/invalid JWT or malformed claims
        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
        api -> page: Authentication error
    else Verified JWT and claims
        app -> app: userId = verified sub; accessTokenHash = SHA-256 exact JWT
        alt Read-only processing completes
            app -> app: Capture fresh server UTC now before credential query; recheck JWT exp
            app -> infra: QUERY - Check active credential and user
            infra -> t_user_access_token: QUERY - Check active credential and user
            activate t_user_access_token
                note right of t_user_access_token
                    SELECT
                        at.user_id
                    FROM authen.t_user_access_token at
                    WHERE at.token = '<sequence.accessTokenHash>'
                    AND at.user_id = '<sequence.userId>'
                    AND at.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                    AND at.expired_at > '<sequence.now>'
                    AND EXISTS (
                        SELECT 1
                        FROM authen.m_user u
                        WHERE u.id = at.user_id
                        AND u.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                    )
                end note
                t_user_access_token -> infra: Return ACTIVE matching token/user or no row
            deactivate t_user_access_token
            infra -> app: Return ACTIVE matching token/user or no row
            alt Credential/user ACTIVE and stored/JWT expiry valid at now
                app -> app: permissionHeld = permission is in verifiedJwt.permissions (exact, case-sensitive)
                alt scope is specified
                    app -> app: scopeHeld = scope is in verifiedJwt.scopes (exact, case-sensitive); allowed = permissionHeld AND scopeHeld
                else scope is omitted
                    app -> app: allowed = permissionHeld; data.scope = null
                end
                app -> app: data.permission and data.scope echo the validated query; no live grant lookup; PLATFORM_ADMIN in roles changes nothing
                note over app, infra
                    Governing decisions: WP5 author design A12 (5b restarted by the owner on 2026-11-17), owner answers of
                    2026-11-17 (Q1–Q6, relayed by Josh) and the owner-confirmed API review Q2/Q4/Q12/Q13. This specification
                    is in-review; no backend implementation is included.
                    Any caller with a valid access token can call this API, and checks only the caller's own token.
                    Q1: the answer comes only from the verified `permissions` and `scopes` claims. Do not query
                    author.t_role_permission, author.t_role_permission_scope, author.t_user_permission, author.t_user_role or
                    any other grant table to reload, add or remove a claim. Grant changes after issuance do not change this
                    token's answer until the token expires or is replaced at refresh (Q2/Q4), which is exactly what a
                    permission-enforcing API decides from the same token.
                    Q2: permission and scope are checked separately. `allowed` is true when the permission claim is in
                    `permissions` and, when `scope` is specified, the scope claim is in `scopes`. The payload is flat (the
                    association of a scope with its permission, Q12, is resolved at login but not carried in the token), so
                    `allowed` does not prove that this scope was granted with this permission.
                    Q3: no implicit permission for PLATFORM_ADMIN; superseding A2, a platform administrator is allowed only what
                    the token holds. The roles claim is validated but never used for the answer.
                    Compare exact, case-sensitive strings; no wildcard, alias, parent namespace or `crud` expansion is inferred.
                    The current token/user check still allows logout/password reset to revoke credentials immediately (Q13).
                    Always HTTP 200 S10000 Check Permission Success with data.permission, data.scope (null when omitted) and
                    data.allowed; a permission the token does not hold is allowed=false, never 403. Never return the claims
                    arrays, stored token hashes or internal credential ids. Timeout returns 408 E90001; unexpected failure
                    returns generic 500 with no bizCode. No outcome writes data.
                end note
                app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 Check Permission Success; data.permission, data.scope, data.allowed
                api -> page: Return the answer for this token
                page -> user: Display whether the token holds the permission
            else Credential/user inactive, revoked, mismatched or expired
                app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                api -> page: Authentication error
            end
        else Timeout during read-only processing
            app -> api: HTTP 408 E90001
            api -> page: Check timed out; no writes
        else Unexpected read-only failure
            app -> api: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error; omit bizCode
            api -> page: Generic check failure; no writes
        end
    end
end
deactivate app
deactivate api
deactivate page
@enduml
